  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/validate.cc",
    "description": "In ValidateArrayDataVisitor::Visit(const UnionArray&), union type codes are validated with `if (code < 0 || child_ids[code] == kInvalidChildId)`, but there is no upper-bound check that `code < child_ids.size()` (or <=255 constraints before indexing child_ids). A crafted UnionArray can supply a positive out-of-range type code, causing out-of-bounds read of `child_ids[code]` and ASan global-buffer-overflow at validate.cc:356.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzed IPC stream is decoded into a RecordBatch containing a (nested) UnionArray (seen during ValidateListArray recursion). During RecordBatch::ValidateFull -> internal::ValidateArrayData, Visit(UnionArray) iterates non-null slots and reads `type_codes[i]`. If an element has a positive type code not present in the union type\u2019s child_ids vector, the validator indexes child_ids with that unchecked code and crashes before returning an Invalid status."
  },
